From: Samin Guo <samin.guo@starfivetech.com>
Subject: [PATCH] dmaengine: dw-axi-dmac: Handle xfer start while non-idle

StarFive's fix, carried by OpenWrt as
1013-dmaengine-dw-axi-dmac-Handle-xfer-start-while-non-id.patch and not
in mainline. Rebased onto Ubuntu-raspi-7.0.0-1017.17.

The behaviour is unchanged from theirs: a start while the channel is
still enabled disables it and programs the transfer, and the error
handler re-issues that descriptor instead of failing it. The shipped
axi_chan_block_xfer_start() does not call axi_dma_enable() — runtime PM
enables the controller from alloc_chan_resources — so that context line
from the OpenWrt patch is not in this rebase. axi_chan_handle_err()
matches upstream 7.0.12.

Signed-off-by: Samin Guo <samin.guo@starfivetech.com>
Signed-off-by: Curry Zhang <curry.zhang@starfivetech.com>
---
--- a/drivers/dma/dw-axi-dmac/dw-axi-dmac-platform.c
+++ b/drivers/dma/dw-axi-dmac/dw-axi-dmac-platform.c
@@ -515,11 +515,13 @@
 	u32 irq_mask;
 	u8 lms = 0; /* Select AXI0 master for LLI fetching */
 
+	chan->is_err = false;
 	if (unlikely(axi_chan_is_hw_enable(chan))) {
 		dev_err(chan2dev(chan), "%s is non-idle!\n",
 			axi_chan_name(chan));
 
-		return;
+		axi_chan_disable(chan);
+		chan->is_err = true;
 	}
 
 	config.dst_multblk_type = DWAXIDMAC_MBLK_TYPE_LL;
@@ -1183,8 +1185,16 @@
 	if (!vd) {
 		dev_err(chan2dev(chan), "BUG: %s, IRQ with no descriptors\n",
 			axi_chan_name(chan));
+		goto out;
+	}
+	if (chan->is_err) {
+		struct axi_dma_desc *desc = vd_to_axi_desc(vd);
+
+		axi_chan_block_xfer_start(chan, desc);
+		chan->is_err = false;
 		goto out;
 	}
+
 	/* Remove the completed descriptor from issued list */
 	list_del(&vd->node);
 
--- a/drivers/dma/dw-axi-dmac/dw-axi-dmac.h
+++ b/drivers/dma/dw-axi-dmac/dw-axi-dmac.h
@@ -50,6 +50,7 @@
 	struct dma_slave_config		config;
 	enum dma_transfer_direction	direction;
 	bool				cyclic;
+	bool				is_err;
 	/* these other elements are all protected by vc.lock */
 	bool				is_paused;
 };
